README.md:3: A signed guestbook visitors leave their mark on, plus an **ed25519 build mark** baked into every page. The wall shows avatar + handle + body, renders admin actions behind a token, and keeps identities separate from the host app's auth.
README.md:7: - **Signed wall** — visitor writes `body` text; identity (avatar, handle) comes from the host's identity resolver.
README.md:8: - **Per-action auth** — no app-wide sign-in wall. Visitors post when they tap the input; signed-out visitors can still post anonymously.
README.md:9: - **Adapter-pattern identity** — hosts provide their own resolver (`presence.identity.resolve`); with no resolver, the wall is silently disabled. The companion `@nuxt-presence/github` ships a built-in GitHub OAuth fallback.
README.md:11: - **Moderation** — graded filter (hard reject / soft pending) with host-extendable blocklists; per-IP / per-user rate limit; token-gated admin tab in the overlay; report endpoint.
README.md:12: - **Social pull** — provider-side connections (e.g. GitHub followers/following) ride on the same identity and surface as badges in the wall.
